# Bounce Trial - BONANZA's course 2 (SPEC.md 128.11.13): the course D4 is judged
# on, built for the RUBBER ball.  Everything wave 2 adds is on it, each where
# the route passes it:
#  - a 6-unit drop off the start tier H onto a floor F four tiles deep, and
#    beyond F a two-tile gap to a ledge G two units ABOVE F.  Only a bounce
#    reaches G: rubber's (a fall of 6 units rebounds at 615, 3.7 units), never
#    steel's (stunned on F: a fall of 2 units or more) nor glass's (shattered
#    on F: 3 or more), and no Hop (4.5 px at most) climbs 2 units.  No up-ramp
#    is within five tiles of the gap (SPEC.md 128.11.5.3);
#  - a STEEP ramp (2 units a tile, r = -4) four tiles long, so a ball thrown
#    off its crest at the cap lands on it, not on its foot;
#  - ICE between BUMPER rails (walls with a bounce surface: 230/256 to every
#    ball), then SAND before the goal;
#  - a MAT (a bounce floor) off the route, beside the steep ramp, 8 units
#    below its crest.
# The gap runs TOWARD THE VIEWER (along +wx): the screen-row layout (the gap
# along a cell row, 128.11.13's shadow row) was tried first and kept its flight
# off every OCC cell, but the autopilot rolls a screen row on ONE arrow, and one
# arrow's top speed (189 - 252 an axis, the round-up drag's dead band) is
# under the 256 its bounce needs to carry the gap - so the route could not
# cross.  This layout's airborne steps over OCC cells are counted instead
# (`bbcourse.py --selfcheck` item 8).
course TRIAL "Bounce Trial"
width  64
ball   rubber

# H, the start tier, 6 units over F
floor rect   4 10  9 13  flat 14
# F, four tiles deep along the route; then the gap, wx 13 and 14
floor rect   9 10 13 13  flat 8
# G, the ledge two units above F, and its far rail
floor rect  15 10 19 13  flat 10
wall  rect  19 10 20 13  flat 10.5
# the steep ramp down from G, along +wy, and its inner rail
floor rect  16 13 19 17  ramp y 13 17 10 2
wall  rect  15 13 16 17  flat 10.5
# the turn at its foot, then the ice back along -wx between bumper rails
floor rect  16 17 19 19  flat 2
floor rect  11 17 16 19  flat 2
surface ice    rect 11 17 16 19
wall  rect  11 16 15 17  flat 2.5
wall  rect   9 19 19 20  flat 2.5
surface bounce rect 11 16 15 17
surface bounce rect 11 19 19 20
# sand before the goal
floor rect   9 17 11 19  flat 2
surface sand   rect  9 17 11 19
goal  rect   8 17  9 19  flat 2
# the mat, off the route beside the steep ramp
floor rect  19 13 21 17  flat 2
surface bounce rect 19 13 21 17

start 5 11

# The autopilot's route (the benchmark's TRIAL leg, SPEC.md 128.11.13): off
# H's lip at speed, its bounces on F carry it over the gap onto G, down the
# steep ramp, back along the ice and over the sand to the goal - no fall in
# 1,289 steps (`bbcourse.py --selfcheck` item 8).
way   5 11
way  17 11
way  17 15
way  17 18
way  13 18
way   8 18

# Wave 4 (SPEC.md 128.14.3.1): par, the autopilot's time on the route (500 steps,
# 9.2 s) and a third, PROVISIONAL (O41).  It writes nothing into the part.
par 12
